{
  "slug": "merge-booking-windows",
  "title": "Merge Booking Windows",
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "statement_md": "A shared room takes bookings as **half-open** time windows `(start, end)`: the room is busy from `start` up to, but not including, `end`. Bookings arrive in no particular order, and they may overlap, nest inside each other, or repeat.\n\nReturn the room's **busy periods**: the smallest list of windows covering exactly the times at least one booking covers, sorted by `start`.\n\nTwo windows that merely **touch**, like `(1, 5)` and `(5, 7)`, leave the room no idle moment, so they merge into `(1, 7)`. Windows separated by any gap, like `(1, 2)` and `(3, 4)`, stay separate.",
  "languages": [
    {"language": "python", "function_name": "merge_bookings", "starter_code": "def merge_bookings(bookings: list[list[int]]) -> list[list[int]]:\n    pass\n", "params": [{"name": "bookings", "type": "list[list[int]]"}]},
